Subject: [PATCH] [mlir][UB] ub.unreachable has no memory effects

`ub.unreachable` declares no memory effects at all, so every reader of
effects takes it as having all of them: a region that ends in it keeps
its parent alive in dead code elimination, and an analysis that sums a
block's effects sees a write to every resource where control never goes
on. The op is undefined behavior when executed, so no effect of it can
be observed: it now declares `NoMemoryEffect`. It stays unspeculatable.
---
diff --git a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.td b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.td
index 1bff39a..f2f3a14 100644
--- a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.td
+++ b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/UB/IR/UBOps.td
@@ -70,11 +70,13 @@ def PoisonOp : UB_Op<"poison", [ConstantLike, Pure]> {
 // UnreachableOp
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
-def UnreachableOp : UB_Op<"unreachable", [Terminator]> {
+def UnreachableOp : UB_Op<"unreachable", [NoMemoryEffect, Terminator]> {
   let summary = "Unreachable operation.";
   let description = [{
     The `unreachable` operation triggers immediate undefined behavior if
-    executed.
+    executed. It reads and writes no memory: a program that reaches it has
+    no defined behavior from that point, so no effect of it can be
+    observed. It is not speculatable.
 
     Example:
 
diff --git a/mlir/test/Dialect/UB/canonicalize.mlir b/mlir/test/Dialect/UB/canonicalize.mlir
index c3f286e..037cbb0 100644
--- a/mlir/test/Dialect/UB/canonicalize.mlir
+++ b/mlir/test/Dialect/UB/canonicalize.mlir
@@ -9,3 +9,16 @@ func.func @merge_poison() -> (i32, i32) {
   %1 = ub.poison : i32
   return %0, %1 : i32, i32
 }
+
+// -----
+
+// ub.unreachable has no memory effects, so a region that does nothing but
+// reach it leaves its parent trivially dead.
+// CHECK-LABEL: func @dead_region_ending_in_unreachable()
+//  CHECK-NEXT:   return
+func.func @dead_region_ending_in_unreachable() {
+  scf.execute_region no_inline {
+    ub.unreachable
+  }
+  return
+}
